  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is the translation of genetic signal into gene-, target- or phenotype-level claims through networks and evidence decomposition. BRIDGE propagates genetic evidence over coupled protein and disease networks and raises target-indication coverage from 5.1% to 9.5%. An Open Targets re-ranking study separates genetic from protein evidence channels for Alzheimer and Parkinson disease associations and reports improved curated-gene recall. A path-energy framework conditions inference over AlzKB and Hetionet on the uncertainty of genomic model predictions to generate phenotype hypotheses. Upstream, variant interpretation remains model-driven. A benchmark of six genomic foundation models on ClinVar variants in LGMD genes finds Evo2 strongest with 501 bp context. SpliceVarMech combines sequence diffusion and Bayesian inference to interpret non-canonical splicing variants. PertiNet, a multimodal model for protein-protein interaction prediction, is adjacent to this thread rather than central to it. The new element is explicit uncertainty-aware and auditable evidence handling.",
